Z||000000||fropuff||10-01-2000||12:08 AM||||Hey, while looking on this website, I accidentally hit my hand on the keyboard.  All of a sudden, the computer "thought" a little, then the print on the site got large.  I must have hit some specific code for AOL.  It doesn't bother me that much, but it is still large when it is printed.  Anybody know?  Thanks.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Patrick||10-01-2000||02:56 AM||||<BR>Assuming that you're running Win9x, click <I>Alt-v</I>. Do you now see <I>Text Size</I> as one of your options? If so, choose whichever size you like.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Cheever2||10-01-2000||02:58 AM||||For a second there I thought you said TEXAS SIZE.  That's the size I like, heheh.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Monkeyman||10-01-2000||08:57 AM||||Same thing happens when you hold CTRL and use the scroll wheel.  Nice feature unless you're really tired and don't realize what you've done.  Works in ME and NT, too.  (ME at home and NT at work.  Boss is very computer illiterate [might be able to turn it on if he was having a very good day].  Small text one day and XXL the next.  hehehe)||||reg||1
Z||000004||fropuff||10-01-2000||10:33 AM||||Thanks guys!  I used the method Monkeyman told me.  Easier.  Now I know how to do this.  Glad I asked.  I didn't mind it, but my dad was.  It wasn't really a big deal, but...  Oh yeah, Monkeyman, how do you feel about getting rid of the FM convertor?  Thanks again.||||reg||1
